        "## Implementing a Real-Life Dataset - Evaluating Median Income vs Median House Price\n",
        "We will now load the **California Housing Dataset** directly from Colab's local file storage (`/content/sample_data/california_housing_train.csv`). This dataset contains real-world census data where we can train a model to predict the `median_house_value` based on actual attributes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gu9xogHgvzUt"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Problem Statement:**\n",
        "We need to predict the **median house value** for the State of California based on the **median income** of the household. This will help in terms of:\n",
        "- Comparing housing prices to local household incomes\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset:** California Housing Dataset (`california_housing_train.csv`) containing columns including:\n",
        "- `median_income` — Independent variable (X) (in tens of thousands of dollars)\n",
        "- `median_house_value` — Dependent variable (Y) ($)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** Build a Regression model that learns the relationship:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ Median\\ House\\ Value = m \\times Median\\ Income + c $$\n",
        "\n",
        "where `m` is the slope and `c` is the intercept."
      ]
    },
